// Calls through a relay's SFU (docs/protocol.md §12).
//
// Media is WebRTC between each participant's client and the call's relay,
// which forwards it to the other participants (a selective forwarding unit)
// without keys: every frame is end-to-end encrypted with SFrame (RFC 9605)
// under call keys only the community server and participants hold.
//
// The relay keeps no accounts or keys. It admits a participant on a grant
// signed by the community server's key, and the call id commits to that key,
// so only that server can grant entry to its calls.

